(6175215, 910453, 61679, '<td valign="top">Great concept and congratulations on your first ribbon.  Another change you could try in your post processing steps is to not do any sharpening until after you size the image to 800 pixels.  I don''t know if your software has Unsharp Mask (USM) but if you do, here are a couple of settings you can use after you size the image.<br/> <br/>Amount 100% Radius 1.0 or Amount 75% and Radius 0.75. <br/> <br/>I find one of these two settings will work after I downsize my image.<br/> <br/>Tim<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-10-03 13:59:54.</i></td>', 'Great concept and congratulations on your first ribbon.  Another change you could try in your post processing steps is to not do any sharpening until after you size the image to 800 pixels.  I don''t know if your software has Unsharp Mask (USM) but if you do, here are a couple of settings you can use after you size the image. Amount 100% Radius 1.0 or Amount 75% and Radius 0.75.  I find one of these two settings will work after I downsize my image. Tim', '2010-09-29 20:30:55.000000', '2010-10-03 14:59:54.000000', 0),
